        "procedure": "A mixture of LiOH·H2O (8.0 mg, 0.2 mmol) and H2L (44.2 mg, 0.1 mmol) in methanol (3 mL) was stirred for 5 min. A solution of Eu(NO3)3·6H2O (35.50 mg, 0.1 mmol) in methanol (8 mL) was then added and the mixture was rapidly stirred for 30 min. Light-yellow crystals suitable for X-ray analysis were obtained by slow evaporation of methanol over one week at room temperature in air (57% yield based on Eu(NO3)3·6H2O).",
